# =============================================================================
# fw_env.config — RK3588 A/B-virt emulator: U-Boot env via FAT file (PWU-AB-2)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT path — the U-Boot env lives as FILE uboot.env on the FAT
# boot partition (GPT p1). Both U-Boot and fw_setenv/fw_printenv access the SAME
# file via different paths:
#   U-Boot: CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT=y -> virtio 0:1 uboot.env  (the bootloader's
#           own filesystem driver reads/writes the file at $loadaddr)
#   Linux:  fw_setenv -> libubootenv -> /boot/uboot.env       (the guest mounts
#           FAT p1 at /boot via /etc/fstab; env is a flat file at offset 0)
#
# Shared dependency of PWU-AB-2 (RAUC slot arm via fw_setenv BOOT_ORDER swap) and
# PWU-AB-4 (healthy-marker bootcount reset) — see PWU_AB_2_RAUC_VERITY.md §4.5
# and PWU_AB_4_APPLY_PORT.md §3.
#
# Format: <path>  <offset>  <env-size>  [<sector-size>]
#   <path>     = absolute path to the env file on a mounted filesystem
#   <offset>   = 0x0000 (start of file — the env data IS the file content)
#   <env-size> = 0x4000 (16384 bytes — MUST match CONFIG_ENV_SIZE)
#
# The file is generated by assemble_ab_disk.sh:
#   mkenvimage -s 0x4000 -o /asm/in/uboot.env.bin /asm/in/uboot.env
# and mcopy'd onto the FAT partition as ::uboot.env.
#
# Sources:
#   https://docs.u-boot.org/en/latest/develop/environment.html
#     (fw_env.config: device, offset, env-size, sector-size)
#   https://gitlab.swupdate.org/stefano/libubootenv/-/blob/main/docs/fw_env_config.md
#     (VFAT file example: /boot/uboot.env 0x0000 0x4000)
#   https://rauc.readthedocs.io/en/latest/integration.html
#     (RAUC reads /etc/fw_env.config for its U-Boot backend)
#   Research: docs/research/20260619-pwu-ab2-linux-path/RESEARCH.md §5 Q4 PATH B
# =============================================================================

# ACTIVE config (CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_FAT, PWU-AB-2):
/boot/uboot.env  0x0000  0x4000
